IMPORT prelude

-- Australian Passports Act 2005 (Commonwealth) -- can I get a passport, whose consent do I need, how long will it last, and
-- what will it cost?
--
-- SEAT: the passport applicant; for a child, the child and the parents (and others) whose consent s 11 requires. Every
-- decision is phrased as that person asks it, from facts they could state. Where the Act speaks to the Minister (ss 8, 11,
-- 12-17, 19A), the encoding says what it means for the applicant: the Minister must not issue, may refuse, or may issue
-- despite a missing consent.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 6(1) ("child"), s 7 (the citizen's entitlement; the form and the fee), s 8 (the Minister's
-- satisfaction of citizenship and identity), s 11 (consent of each person with parental responsibility, the court-order
-- alternative, the exceptions in s 11(2), the meaning of parental responsibility in s 11(5)), s 12(2) (must not issue after a
-- law-enforcement request), ss 13(2), 14(2), 15, 16(2) (may refuse), s 17 (a document already valid or suspended), s 19 (stale
-- or withdrawn requests), s 19A (refusal to process; the fee is kept), s 20 (when a document stops being valid), s 48
-- (reviewable decisions), s 49(2) (28 days to seek review of a delegate's decision).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 21, compilation date 8 November 2025 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 60, 2025"; register id
-- C2025C00643), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2005A00005.txt (retrieved 2026-10-13).
-- Instruments used:
--   Australian Passports Determination 2015, Compilation No. 7, compilation date 13 June 2026 ("Includes amendments:
--   F2026L00715"; register id F2026C00500), as deposited at
--   ../../../australian-passports-determination-2015/registers/source-bundle/F2015L01223.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19):
--   s 10 (special circumstances, s 11(2)(a)), s 15 (concurrent documents, s 17(2)), s 16 (diplomatic and official), s 17
--   (maximum periods of validity, s 20(2)), ss 18-19 (damage, death, loss of citizenship), s 27(1)(a), (k), (l) (waivers),
--   s 28A (no waiver after a refusal/cancellation request), s 31 (the 2005 Determination for earlier applications).
--   Australian Passports (Application Fees) Determination 2015, Compilation No. 5, compilation date 26 November 2024
--   ("Includes amendments: F2024L01494"; register id F2024C01230), as deposited at
--   ../../../australian-passports-application-fees-determination-2015/registers/source-bundle/F2015L01222.txt (retrieved
--   2026-10-19): s 5 (application fees, items 1-6), s 6 (additional fees, items 1-4), s 7 (indexation; the factor itself is an
--   INPUT, because the formula is an image the deposit does not carry and the CPI numbers are not deposited).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: travel-related documents (ss 9, 10; Determination ss 6-9) beyond the word; who the competent authorities are
-- and when they may make a refusal/cancellation request (ss 12(1), (1A), 13(1), 14(1), 16(1), 18; Determination ss 11-14) --
-- the request is an INPUT, and only its effect on the applicant is encoded; cancellation, suspension and surrender
-- (ss 22-26); the offences (Part 4); information and disclosure (ss 42-47); names (s 53; Determination s 25); refunds
-- (Determination s 28); notice (s 48A); the Tribunal's powers (s 50); delegation and determinations (ss 51, 52, 57, 58). The
-- text of s 11 before the 2015 amendment (No 122, 2015) and the Australian Passports Determination 2005, which Determination
-- s 31 keeps for applications lodged before 1 October 2015, are not deposited: Chloe's 2011 application is answered on the
-- text deposited, and her fee is reported as not set by this edition. Fees for years before 2024 are not in the deposited
-- compilation.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use as advice. Dates
-- are numbers written YYYYMMDD. Judgments the Act hands to the Minister are INPUTS ("if the Minister is satisfied that ...").

§ `Australian Passports Act 2005`

§§ `6(1) -- am I a child`

-- s 6(1): "child means a person who is under 18 and who has never been married."
@export Am I a child for the purposes of the Australian Passports Act (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `I have ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been married (even if no longer)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a child` IF
    `my age` < 18 AND (NOT `I have ever been married`)

§§ `11(5) -- who has parental responsibility for me`

-- s 11(5): "a person has parental responsibility for a child if, and only if: (a) the person: (i) is the child's parent
-- (including a person who is presumed to be the child's parent because of a presumption (other than in section 69Q) in ...
-- the Family Law Act 1975); and (ii) has not ceased to have parental responsibility for the child because of an order made
-- under the Family Law Act 1975; or (aa) the person: (i) is the child's parent (including ... a presumption (other than in
-- section 189) in ... the Family Court Act 1997 (WA)); and (ii) has not ceased to have parental responsibility for the child
-- because of an order made under that Act; or (b) under a parenting order: (i) the child is to live with the person; or
-- (ii) the person has parental responsibility for the child; or (d) the person has guardianship or custody of, or has
-- parental responsibility for, the child under a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory."
-- "Parent", "parenting order" and the presumptions are borrowed from the family law Acts and asked as facts. Read literally,
-- (a) and (aa) are alternatives: a parent loses parental responsibility for passport purposes only when orders under BOTH
-- Acts have removed it. (Whether a court would read the limbs as covering different children is an inference not tested.)
DECLARE `Person with a say` HAS
    `is my parent` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Is your parent (including a person presumed to be your parent under the Family Law Act 1975 or the Family Court Act 1997 (WA))
    `lost parental responsibility by a Family Law Act 1975 order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lost parental responsibility by a Family Court Act 1997 (WA) order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am to live with them under a parenting order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has parental responsibility under a parenting order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has guardianship, custody or parental responsibility under another law` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does this person have parental responsibility for me, so that their consent is needed (s 11(5))?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Person with a say` @desc The person you are asking about, and the orders that affect them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this person have parental responsibility for me` IF
        (`the person`'s `is my parent` AND (NOT `the person`'s `lost parental responsibility by a Family Law Act 1975 order`))
    OR  (`the person`'s `is my parent` AND (NOT `the person`'s `lost parental responsibility by a Family Court Act 1997 (WA) order`))
    OR  `the person`'s `I am to live with them under a parenting order`
    OR  `the person`'s `has parental responsibility under a parenting order`
    OR  `the person`'s `has guardianship, custody or parental responsibility under another law`

§§ `11(2)(a) and Determination s 10 -- special circumstances`

-- Determination s 10(3): "(a) the Minister has not been able to contact the non-consenting person for a reasonable period;
-- (b) the non-consenting person is either or both of the following: (i) missing; (ii) presumed dead; (c) the non-consenting
-- person is medically incapable of providing consent; (d) there has been no contact between the child and the
-- non-consenting person for a substantial period before the application is made; (e) the non-consenting person: (i) is not
-- an Australian citizen; and (ii) is separated from a person who has parental responsibility for the child and has consented
-- ...; and (iii) has not had contact with the child since the child arrived in Australia; (f) a family violence order has
-- been issued against the non-consenting person; (g) if the child is outside Australia--there is evidence of family
-- violence; (h) an order of a court in a convention country ... permits ...; (i) if the child is outside Australia--the
-- Minister considers that there is a need for the child to travel internationally or the child requires a travel document
-- to continue to legally reside overseas; (j) an order of a State or Territory court, made under a child welfare law, grants
-- parental responsibility or guardianship of the child to: (i) a parent of the child other than the non-consenting person;
-- or (ii) a person other than a parent of the child."
-- Determination s 10(2): s 10(1) "does not apply if the Minister has been provided with court documents demonstrating that
-- there are proceedings before a Commonwealth, State or Territory court that may affect: (aa) the issue of an Australian
-- travel document to the child; or (a) the rights of the child to travel internationally; or (b) who has parental
-- responsibility for the child."
DECLARE `Special circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `none of the special circumstances`
    `the Minister could not contact the non-consenting person for a reasonable period`
    `the non-consenting person is missing or presumed dead`
    `the non-consenting person is medically incapable of consenting`
    `no contact between me and the non-consenting person for a substantial period`
    `the non-consenting person is a non-citizen, separated, with no contact since I arrived in Australia`
    `a family violence order against the non-consenting person`
    `I am outside Australia and there is evidence of family violence`
    `a convention-country court order permits my document, travel or contact abroad`
    `I am outside Australia and the Minister considers I need to travel or need a document to stay lawfully`
    `a child welfare order gives parental responsibility or guardianship to someone else`

-- (g) and (i) apply only "if the child is outside Australia".
@export Is there a special circumstance in which a passport can be issued to me without a parent's consent (s 11(2)(a), Determination s 10)?
GIVEN `the circumstance` IS A `Special circumstance` @desc Which of the circumstances in Determination s 10(3) exists, if any
      `I am outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are outside Australia
      `court documents about proceedings were given to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has been given court documents showing proceedings that may affect your passport, your travel or who has parental responsibility for you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a special circumstance for me` IF
    (NOT `court documents about proceedings were given to the Minister`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the circumstance`
         WHEN `none of the special circumstances` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `I am outside Australia and there is evidence of family violence` THEN `I am outside Australia`
         WHEN `I am outside Australia and the Minister considers I need to travel or need a document to stay lawfully` THEN `I am outside Australia`
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `7, 8, 11, 12-17, 19, 19A -- my application for a passport`

DECLARE `Passport application` HAS
    `application date` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The date you apply, written YYYYMMDD
    `my age` IS A NUMBER
    `I have ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied I am an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied of my identity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicable fee is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `people with parental responsibility for me` IS A NUMBER
    `of them, how many consent` IS A NUMBER
    `a court order permits my document, my international travel, or my living or spending time with someone abroad` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the special circumstance` IS A `Special circumstance`
    `court documents about proceedings were given to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied my welfare would suffer if I could not travel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied I urgently need to travel because of a family crisis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a non-consenting person cannot be contacted within a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have departed Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months from my departure to the application` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister considers a document should issue for my return` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a section 12 request has been made about me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a section 13, 14 or 16 request has been made about me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the request has been withdrawn or is no longer current` IS A BOOLEAN
    `travel documents of mine lost or stolen in the 5 years before` IS A NUMBER
    `I already hold an Australian travel document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date on that document` IS A NUMBER
    `that document has been cancelled or has ceased under the Determination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that document is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a concurrent-document circumstance in Determination s 15 or 16 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister suspects a false or misleading statement, information or document` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 11(1): "The Minister must not issue an Australian travel document to a child unless: (a) each person who has parental
-- responsibility for the child consents to the child having an Australian travel document; or (b) an order of a court of the
-- Commonwealth, a State or a Territory permits: (i) the child to have an Australian travel document; or (ii) the child to
-- travel internationally; or (iii) the child to live or spend time with another person who is outside Australia."
-- "Each person" read literally: if no-one has parental responsibility, (a) is met.
GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `everyone's consent or a court order is in place` IF
        `a`'s `of them, how many consent` >= `a`'s `people with parental responsibility for me`
    OR  `a`'s `a court order permits my document, my international travel, or my living or spending time with someone abroad`

-- s 11(2): "Subsection (1) does not prevent the Minister from issuing an Australian travel document to a child if: (a)
-- circumstances specified in a Minister's determination as special circumstances exist; or (b) the Minister is satisfied that
-- the child's welfare (physical or psychological) would be adversely affected if the child were not able to travel
-- internationally; or (c) the Minister is satisfied that: (i) the child urgently needs to travel internationally because of a
-- family crisis; and (ii) if there is a person who has parental responsibility for the child and who has not consented ...--it
-- is not possible to contact that person within a reasonable period; or (d) in the case of a child who is outside
-- Australia--the child departed Australia less than 12 months before the application ... was made and the Minister considers
-- that an Australian travel document should be issued to enable the child's return to Australia."
-- These permit; they do not oblige ("does not prevent"). (d) needs a departure, so a child born abroad cannot use it.
@export Can a passport be issued to me even though not everyone with parental responsibility consents (s 11(2))?
GIVEN `my application` IS A `Passport application` @desc The facts of your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I get a passport without everyone's consent` IF
        `Is there a special circumstance for me` (`my application`'s `the special circumstance`) (`my application`'s `I am outside Australia`)
            (`my application`'s `court documents about proceedings were given to the Minister`)
    OR  `my application`'s `the Minister is satisfied my welfare would suffer if I could not travel`
    OR  (    `my application`'s `the Minister is satisfied I urgently need to travel because of a family crisis`
         AND `my application`'s `a non-consenting person cannot be contacted within a reasonable period`)
    OR  (    `my application`'s `I am outside Australia`
         AND `my application`'s `I have departed Australia`
         AND `my application`'s `months from my departure to the application` < 12
         AND `my application`'s `the Minister considers a document should issue for my return`)

@export Does the consent rule in s 11 stop a passport being issued to me?
GIVEN `my application` IS A `Passport application` @desc The facts of your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does s 11 stop my passport` IF
        `Am I a child` (`my application`'s `my age`) (`my application`'s `I have ever been married`)
    AND (NOT `everyone's consent or a court order is in place` `my application`)
    AND (NOT `Can I get a passport without everyone's consent` `my application`)

-- s 19: "The Minister must not act on a refusal/cancellation request if that request: (a) has been withdrawn by the competent
-- authority who made it; or (b) can no longer be regarded as current in accordance with the Department's usual
-- administrative practices."
GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a live section 12 request` IF
    `a`'s `a section 12 request has been made about me` AND (NOT `a`'s `the request has been withdrawn or is no longer current`)

GIVEN `a` IS A `Passport application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a live section 13, 14 or 16 request` IF
    `a`'s `a section 13, 14 or 16 request has been made about me` AND (NOT `a`'s `the request has been withdrawn or is no longer current`)

-- s 20(1): "An Australian travel document ceases to be valid: (a) in accordance with a determination made for the purposes of
-- subsection (2); or (b) at the time specified on the document; or (c) when cancelled under this Division; whichever happens
-- first." (3): "An Australian travel document is not valid while it is suspended under section 22A."
-- Determination s 18: a document ceases to be valid if "it is damaged; and ... the Minister is satisfied that it is no longer
-- usable"; s 19(1): on the occurrence of a circumstance in an endorsement or written advice; s 19(2): "if the holder of the
-- travel document dies or loses his or her Australian citizenship."
-- A document is treated as having ceased ON the date specified (an inference about "at the time specified").
@export Is my Australian passport still valid on this date (s 20, Determination ss 18-19)?
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER @desc The date asked about, written YYYYMMDD
      `the date on my passport` IS A NUMBER @desc The date of expiry printed on the passport, written YYYYMMDD
      `it has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the passport has been cancelled
      `it is suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the passport is suspended under s 22A
      `it is damaged and the Minister is satisfied it is unusable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is damaged and the Minister is satisfied it can no longer be used as evidence of identity and citizenship or for travel
      `I have lost my Australian citizenship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have lost your Australian citizenship
      `an endorsed circumstance has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether something the passport or a written notice said would end its validity has happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my passport still valid` IF
        `the date` < `the date on my passport`
    AND (NOT `it has been cancelled`)
    AND (NOT `it is suspended`)
    AND (NOT `it is damaged and the Minister is satisfied it is unusable`)
    AND (NOT `I have lost my Australian citizenship`)
    AND (NOT `an endorsed circumstance has happened`)

-- s 17(1): "The Minister must not issue an Australian travel document to a person if the person has already been issued with
-- an Australian travel document and that document is still valid or is suspended under section 22A." (2): not "in the
-- circumstances specified in a Minister's determination" -- Determination s 15 (a second document to avoid visa delays; a
-- country that will not accept evidence of travel to another; other exceptional circumstances) and s 16 (diplomatic or
-- official travel, and dependants).
@export Does a travel document I already hold stop a new one being issued (s 17)?
GIVEN `my application` IS A `Passport application` @desc The facts of your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my current document stop a new one` IF
        `my application`'s `I already hold an Australian travel document`
    AND (    `Is my passport still valid` (`my application`'s `application date`) (`my application`'s `the date on that document`)
                 (`my application`'s `that document has been cancelled or has ceased under the Determination`) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
         OR  `my application`'s `that document is suspended`)
    AND (NOT `my application`'s `a concurrent-document circumstance in Determination s 15 or 16 applies`)

-- s 8: "Before issuing an Australian passport to a person, the Minister must be satisfied: (a) that the person is an
-- Australian citizen; and (b) of the identity of the person."
-- s 12(2): "If a competent authority makes a request under subsection (1) or (1A), the Minister must not issue an Australian
-- passport to the person".
@export Must the Minister refuse me a passport (ss 8, 11, 12(2), 17)?
GIVEN `my application` IS A `Passport application` @desc The facts of your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be refused a passport` IF
        (NOT `my application`'s `the Minister is satisfied I am an Australian citizen`)
    OR  (NOT `my application`'s `the Minister is satisfied of my identity`)
    OR  `Does s 11 stop my passport` `my application`
    OR  `a live section 12 request` `my application`
    OR  `Does my current document stop a new one` `my application`

-- s 13(2), 14(2), 16(2): after a request, "the Minister may refuse to issue"; s 15: "The Minister may refuse to issue an
-- Australian travel document to a person if: (a) an application for an Australian travel document is under consideration;
-- and (b) in the 5 years before the application is made, 2 or more Australian travel documents issued to the person have been
-- lost or stolen."
@export May the Minister refuse me a passport, at the Minister's discretion (ss 13-16)?
GIVEN `my application` IS A `Passport application` @desc The facts of your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be refused a passport` IF
        `a live section 13, 14 or 16 request` `my application`
    OR  `my application`'s `travel documents of mine lost or stolen in the 5 years before` >= 2

-- The outcome, as the applicant meets it.
-- s 19A(1): "The Minister may refuse to process an application ... if the Minister suspects, on reasonable grounds, that" a
-- statement, information or document given in or in connection with it is "false or misleading"; (2): "the applicable fee
-- (if any) accompanying the application is not refundable"; (3): "a fresh application is required".
-- s 7(1): "An Australian citizen is entitled, on application to the Minister, to be issued with an Australian passport by the
-- Minister." (2): the entitlement "is affected by section 8 and by Division 2". (3): the application "must be: (a) made in the
-- form approved by the Minister; and (b) accompanied by the applicable fee (if any)."
DECLARE `What happens to my application` IS ONE OF
    `it may not be processed, the fee is kept and I must apply afresh`
    `it is not a valid application: the approved form and the fee are needed`
    `I have no entitlement: only an Australian citizen is entitled`
    `the Minister must not issue me a passport`
    `I am entitled, but the Minister may refuse me`
    `I am entitled to be issued a passport`

@export What happens to my application for an Australian passport (ss 7, 8, 11-17, 19A)?
GIVEN `my application` IS A `Passport application` @desc The facts of your application
GIVETH A `What happens to my application`
DECIDE `What happens to my application for a passport` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `my application`'s `the Minister suspects a false or misleading statement, information or document`
            THEN `it may not be processed, the fee is kept and I must apply afresh`
        IF (NOT `my application`'s `made in the approved form`) OR (NOT `my application`'s `the applicable fee is paid`)
            THEN `it is not a valid application: the approved form and the fee are needed`
        IF (NOT `my application`'s `I am an Australian citizen`)
            THEN `I have no entitlement: only an Australian citizen is entitled`
        IF `Must I be refused a passport` `my application`
            THEN `the Minister must not issue me a passport`
        IF `May I be refused a passport` `my application`
            THEN `I am entitled, but the Minister may refuse me`
        OTHERWISE `I am entitled to be issued a passport`

@export Am I entitled to be issued an Australian passport, with nothing in the Act standing in the way (s 7)?
GIVEN `my application` IS A `Passport application` @desc The facts of your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a passport` IF
    `What happens to my application for a passport` `my application` EQUALS `I am entitled to be issued a passport`

§§ `20(2) and Determination ss 17, 31 -- how long my passport lasts`

-- Determination s 31: "the old determination ... continues to apply in relation to: ... (b) an application ... for the issue
-- of an Australian travel document in any other circumstance that is lodged before that repeal." Endnote 3: the 2015
-- Determination commenced 1 Oct 2015 (the 2005 Determination's repeal date is inferred to be the same day).
@export Is my application governed by the Australian Passports Determination 2015 rather than the 2005 one (Determination s 31)?
GIVEN `application date` IS A NUMBER @desc The date you lodged the application, written YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the 2015 Determination govern my application` IF
    `application date` >= 20151001

-- Determination s 17(2) table: item 1 "issued to an adult and no other item of this table applies" -- 10 years; item 2 "to a
-- child and no other item ... applies" -- 5 years; item 3 "to a child who is 16 or 17 and no other later item ... applies" --
-- 10 years; item 4 "to a person who is 75 or over and no other later item ... applies" -- 5 years; item 5 "a concurrent
-- passport issued ... in a circumstance mentioned in section 15" -- 3 years; item 6 "an emergency passport" -- 1 year; item 7
-- on resigning a diplomatic or official position overseas -- 1 year; item 8 travel for gender reassignment, issued in the
-- intended gender -- 1 year; item 9 "a terminally ill child or an accompanying family member" for charity-sponsored travel --
-- 1 year; item 10 travel documents "lost or stolen: (a) 2 times in the 5 years ... or (b) 3 or more times" -- 5 years or 2
-- years; items 11-17 replacement passports -- "the period ending when the travel document being replaced would otherwise have
-- ceased to be valid" (item 11 only if no other document was lost, stolen or damaged in the 5 years).
-- s 17(3): a document "found and returned", or excused for exceptional circumstances, "is taken not to have been lost or
-- stolen" -- the count asked for is after that.
-- Order: a replacement passport (items 11-17) unless item 10 applies; then item 10; then items 5-9; then items 4, 3, 2, 1.
-- That later items displace earlier ones is read from "no other (later) item"; that item 10 displaces items 5-9 is an inference.
DECLARE `Kind of passport` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary passport`
    `a concurrent passport under Determination s 15`
    `an emergency passport`
    `a passport on resigning a diplomatic or official position overseas`
    `a passport for travel for gender reassignment`
    `a passport for charity-sponsored travel of a terminally ill child or family member`
    `a replacement passport`

DECLARE `Period of validity` IS ONE OF
    `up to` HAS `years` IS A NUMBER
    `until the passport replaced would have expired`

@export What is the longest my passport can be valid for (s 20(2), Determination s 17)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when the passport is issued
      `I have ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been married
      `the kind of passport` IS A `Kind of passport` @desc The kind of passport being issued
      `documents lost or stolen in the 5 years before` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your Australian travel documents were lost or stolen in the 5 years before you applied (not counting one found and returned)
GIVETH A `Period of validity`
DECIDE `How long can my passport be valid` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of passport` EQUALS `a replacement passport` AND `documents lost or stolen in the 5 years before` < 2
            THEN `until the passport replaced would have expired`
        IF `documents lost or stolen in the 5 years before` >= 3 THEN `up to` 2
        IF `documents lost or stolen in the 5 years before` EQUALS 2 THEN `up to` 5
        IF `the kind of passport` EQUALS `a concurrent passport under Determination s 15` THEN `up to` 3
        IF `the kind of passport` EQUALS `an emergency passport` THEN `up to` 1
        IF `the kind of passport` EQUALS `a passport on resigning a diplomatic or official position overseas` THEN `up to` 1
        IF `the kind of passport` EQUALS `a passport for travel for gender reassignment` THEN `up to` 1
        IF `the kind of passport` EQUALS `a passport for charity-sponsored travel of a terminally ill child or family member` THEN `up to` 1
        IF `my age` >= 75 THEN `up to` 5
        IF `Am I a child` `my age` `I have ever been married` AND `my age` >= 16 THEN `up to` 10
        IF `Am I a child` `my age` `I have ever been married` THEN `up to` 5
        OTHERWISE `up to` 10

-- The latest date the passport can carry: the issue date plus the maximum period (YYYYMMDD arithmetic, adding whole years;
-- an inference -- the Determination sets a period, and the date printed is the Minister's).
@export What is the latest expiry date my passport can carry (Determination s 17)?
GIVEN `issue date` IS A NUMBER @desc The date the passport is issued, written YYYYMMDD
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when the passport is issued
      `I have ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been married
      `the kind of passport` IS A `Kind of passport` @desc The kind of passport being issued
      `documents lost or stolen in the 5 years before` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your travel documents were lost or stolen in the 5 years before you applied
      `expiry date of the passport replaced` IS A NUMBER @desc For a replacement passport, the date the passport being replaced would have expired, written YYYYMMDD
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the latest expiry date of my passport` IS
    CONSIDER `How long can my passport be valid` `my age` `I have ever been married` `the kind of passport` `documents lost or stolen in the 5 years before`
    WHEN `up to` n THEN `issue date` + n * 10000
    WHEN `until the passport replaced would have expired` THEN `expiry date of the passport replaced`

§§ `7(3)(b), Application Fees Determination ss 5-7 -- what my passport costs`

-- Fees Determination s 5(3) table (2024 amounts): item 1 "an Australian passport that is valid for up to 10 years" $398;
-- item 2 "for a child that is valid for up to 5 years" $201; item 3 "for a child who is 16 or 17 ... valid for up to 10
-- years" $398; item 4 "by a person who is 75 or over ... valid for up to 5 years" $201; item 5 "an emergency passport" $250;
-- item 6 "a replacement passport" $250.
DECLARE `Fee item` IS ONE OF
    `a 10-year passport`
    `a 5-year passport for a child`
    `a 10-year passport for a child of 16 or 17`
    `a 5-year passport at 75 or over`
    `an emergency passport fee`
    `a replacement passport fee`

GIVEN `the item` IS A `Fee item`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2024 application fee` IS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `a 10-year passport` THEN 398
    WHEN `a 5-year passport for a child` THEN 201
    WHEN `a 10-year passport for a child of 16 or 17` THEN 398
    WHEN `a 5-year passport at 75 or over` THEN 201
    WHEN `an emergency passport fee` THEN 250
    WHEN `a replacement passport fee` THEN 250

-- Which item an ordinary (not emergency, not replacement) application falls under. A child under 16 can have only item 2; a
-- child of 16 or 17 may ask for the 5-year child passport (item 2) instead of item 3; a person 75 or over may pay for either
-- (Determination s 17, Note 1: "a person 75 years or over may pay for a 5 year passport or a 10 year passport").
@export Which application fee item applies to my ordinary passport application (Fees Determination s 5)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when you apply
      `I have ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been married
      `I ask for the shorter 5-year passport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, being 16 or 17 or 75 or over, you ask for a 5-year passport
GIVETH A `Fee item`
DECIDE `Which fee item applies to me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `Am I a child` `my age` `I have ever been married` AND `my age` < 16 THEN `a 5-year passport for a child`
        IF `Am I a child` `my age` `I have ever been married` AND `I ask for the shorter 5-year passport` THEN `a 5-year passport for a child`
        IF `Am I a child` `my age` `I have ever been married` THEN `a 10-year passport for a child of 16 or 17`
        IF `my age` >= 75 AND `I ask for the shorter 5-year passport` THEN `a 5-year passport at 75 or over`
        OTHERWISE `a 10-year passport`

-- Fees Determination s 5(1): for 2024, the table amount; "(b) for an application made in a later calendar year: (i) if the
-- indexation factor for the calendar year is less than 1--the fee ... for the previous calendar year; or (ii) otherwise--the
-- amount worked out by multiplying the indexation factor for the calendar year by the amount of the fee ... for the previous
-- calendar year." (4): "rounded to the nearest whole dollar (rounding 50 cents upwards)". s 6(1) and (5) say the same of the
-- additional fees. s 7: the factor comes from the All Groups CPI; the formula is not in the deposited text (an image) and the
-- CPI numbers are not deposited, so the factors are INPUTS, one per year from 2025 to the year of the application, in order.
-- Each year's fee is read as the rounded amount (an inference: (4) rounds "amounts worked out under this section").
GIVEN `factors` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the fee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `indexed` `factors` `the fee` IS
    CONSIDER `factors`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the fee`
    WHEN f FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN
        `indexed` `rest` (IF f < 1 THEN `the fee` ELSE TRUNC (`the fee` * f + 0.5) 0)

-- The deposited compilation gives no amount for an application before 2024 (s 5 was substituted in 2018 and amended in 2024),
-- so for an earlier year the answer says so.
DECLARE `Fee` IS ONE OF
    `dollars` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `not set by the deposited edition (an application before 2024)`

-- Fees Determination s 6(3): item 1 priority processing (within 2 business days) $290; item 2 fast tracking (within 5 business
-- days) $100; item 3 priority after a fast-track fee was paid $190; item 4 "Application for an Australian passport (other than
-- an emergency passport, a replacement passport or a passport for which the period of validity is less than the maximum period
-- for a passport of that kind) that is made overseas (a) for an adult--$178; and (b) for a child--$87". Note: (a) "includes
-- persons who are 75 or over (regardless of the period of validity ...)" and (b) "includes a child who is 16 or 17 (regardless
-- of the period of validity ...)". s 6(4): "The fee is in addition to the fee (if any) specified under section 5".
DECLARE `Processing speed` IS ONE OF
    `ordinary processing`
    `priority processing`
    `fast tracking`
    `priority processing after paying for fast tracking`

GIVEN `the speed` IS A `Processing speed`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2024 speed fee` IS
    CONSIDER `the speed`
    WHEN `ordinary processing` THEN 0
    WHEN `priority processing` THEN 290
    WHEN `fast tracking` THEN 100
    WHEN `priority processing after paying for fast tracking` THEN 190

GIVEN `the item` IS A `Fee item`
      `I am a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `applying overseas` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2024 overseas fee` IS
    IF (NOT `applying overseas`) OR `the item` EQUALS `an emergency passport fee` OR `the item` EQUALS `a replacement passport fee`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `I am a child` THEN 87 ELSE 178

@export What will my passport application cost, in dollars (s 7(3)(b), Fees Determination ss 5-7)?
GIVEN `the item` IS A `Fee item` @desc The kind of application (see Which fee item applies to me)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when you apply
      `I have ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been married
      `applying overseas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application is made overseas
      `the speed` IS A `Processing speed` @desc Whether you pay for priority processing or fast tracking
      `year of application` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which you apply
      `indexation factors` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The indexation factor for each year from 2025 to the year you apply, in order (empty for 2024)
GIVETH A `Fee`
DECIDE `What will my passport cost` IS
    IF `year of application` < 2024
    THEN `not set by the deposited edition (an application before 2024)`
    ELSE `dollars` (    `indexed` `indexation factors` (`the 2024 application fee` `the item`)
                    +   `indexed` `indexation factors` (`the 2024 speed fee` `the speed`)
                    +   `indexed` `indexation factors`
                            (`the 2024 overseas fee` `the item` (`Am I a child` `my age` `I have ever been married`) `applying overseas`))

-- Determination s 27(1): "the Minister may waive a fee in any of the following circumstances: (a) ... an application for a
-- replacement passport for a child under 5 who has previously been issued with an Australian passport during his or her first
-- year of life, if the child has not previously been issued with a replacement passport; ... (k) ... a passport of a kind
-- mentioned in item 4 of the table in subsection 6(3) of the [Fees Determination] (overseas applications); (l) the Minister is
-- satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist in relation to the applicant." s 28A: "Paragraph 27(1)(l) ... do[es] not
-- apply to a fee for an application ... refused because of a refusal/cancellation request." Only (a), (k) and (l) are encoded.
DECLARE `Waiver ground` IS ONE OF
    `no waiver ground`
    `a replacement for a child under 5 first issued a passport in the first year of life, never replaced before`
    `the overseas application fee`
    `the Minister is satisfied there are exceptional circumstances`

@export May my passport fee be waived (Determination ss 27, 28A)?
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Waiver ground` @desc The ground on which you seek a waiver
      `refused because of a refusal/cancellation request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application was refused because of a refusal/cancellation request
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my fee be waived` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `no waiver ground` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Minister is satisfied there are exceptional circumstances` THEN (NOT `refused because of a refusal/cancellation request`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `48, 49 -- can I have a decision reviewed`

-- s 48: reviewable decisions include "(a) a decision to issue an Australian travel document, other than: (i) a decision made
-- under paragraph 9(1A)(b); or (ii) a decision to issue an Australian travel document to a child; (b) a decision to refuse to
-- issue an Australian travel document (other than a decision in relation to which a declaration under subsection 11(3) has
-- been made or a decision made because of subsection 12(2)); (c) a decision to cancel an Australian travel document (other
-- than under section 22AA); (ca) a decision to refuse to process an application ...; (i) a decision not to waive an application
-- fee ...; (j) a decision not to refund an application fee ...".
-- s 11(3): on refusing a child, "the Minister may declare that he or she is refusing to exercise the discretion under
-- subsection (2) because the matter should be dealt with by a court."
DECLARE `Decision about me` IS ONE OF
    `a decision to issue me a passport as an adult`
    `a decision to issue me a passport as a child`
    `a decision to refuse me a passport`
    `a decision to cancel my passport under s 22`
    `a decision to cancel my passport under s 22AA`
    `a decision to refuse to process my application`
    `a decision not to waive my fee`
    `a decision not to refund my fee`

@export Can I have this passport decision reviewed (s 48)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision about me` @desc The decision made about you
      `a s 11(3) declaration was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister declared that your matter should be dealt with by a court (s 11(3))
      `refused because of s 12(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the refusal was because of a law-enforcement request under s 12
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I have the decision reviewed` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision to issue me a passport as a child` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a decision to refuse me a passport` THEN (NOT `a s 11(3) declaration was made`) AND (NOT `refused because of s 12(2)`)
    WHEN `a decision to cancel my passport under s 22AA` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 49(2): "An application for review of a decision must be made within 28 days after the person is notified of the
-- decision." (A delegate's reviewable decision goes first to the Minister, s 49(1); the Minister's to the Tribunal, s 50.)
@export How many days after being told of a delegate's decision do I have to ask the Minister to review it (s 49(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days do I have to seek review` IS 28
